# Model display names and recognition notes (untranslated languages fall back to the built-in Chinese text)
sku.g533.display = ASUS ROG Strix SCAR 6 / Strix G6, 15", 2022 (G533Z* / G513R*)
sku.g533.note = Module ASUE1403 / ELAN1403 → layout GH2XLNDZ (same family). Only the 2022 generation (Strix SCAR 6 G533Z*, Strix G6 15" G513R*) has a NumberPad; the 2021 generation (G533Q* / G513Q* / G513I*) has no such hardware in its official specs, so `excludes` keeps it out of recognition instead of folding it into this profile. Not every 2022 configuration has it either: 3 of the 5 official Strix G6 configurations are the 4-zone RGB variant without this hardware
sku.g614.display = ASUS ROG Strix SCAR 7 / SCAR 8 and Extreme editions, 16", 2023–2024 (G614 / G634)
sku.g614.note = G614 and G634 share one touchpad (ASUE1416 / ASUF1416 → GH3XLNDZ); a matching model prefix does not guarantee the hardware: 2 of the 10 official 2023 configurations are the 4-zone RGB variant (suffix EACX) without a NumberPad, which covers the whole China-market 魔霸新锐 line. When FEATURE 0x0d is not found at startup the driver treats the machine as incompatible and refuses to run
sku.g615.display = ASUS ROG Strix SCAR 9 / SCAR 10 and Extreme editions, 16", 2025–2026 (G615 / G635)
sku.g615.note = PixArt ASCP1400 / ASCF1400 → GH4XLNDZ (same family). G615 is the standard model and G635 the Extreme edition; the 2026 SCAR 10 reuses the same pair of module ids, whose values come from the 2025 generation. 1 of the 25 official 2025 configurations (90NR0LJ1-M005P0) is the 4-zone RGB variant without a NumberPad, as is the China-market 魔霸新锐 2025 (G614PM / G614PR 8940HX and the Intel versions). The ProArt P16 (H7606) of that generation uses a DialPad knob rather than a NumberPad and is not folded into this profile
sku.gx550.display = ASUS ROG Zephyrus Duo, 15" / 16", side-mounted touchpad (GX550 / GX551 / GX650)
sku.gx550.note = GX550 / GX551 / GX650 all belong to the gx551 key family; module ASUE1408 → GVM_A, ASUE1404 → GVM. GVM_A and GVM share one parameter set (the official NUMPADLAYOUT_GVM_* list stops at _06 and the remaining fields default to 0); layout status: same family, not verified on real hardware. The touchpad sits vertically to the right of the keyboard and numeric mode is toggled by a dedicated keyboard key, not by a long press on the icon area (see README, dual-screen models)
sku.ux582.display = ASUS Zenbook Pro Duo, side-mounted touchpad (UX582 / UX482)
sku.ux582.note = Module ASUE1406 / ELAN1406 → layout NVM (the official NUMPADLAYOUT_NVM_* list stops at _12 and the remaining fields default to 0); layout status: same family, not verified on real hardware. The touchpad sits to the right of the keyboard and numeric mode is toggled by a dedicated keyboard key, not by a long press on the icon area
